#: src/introduction.md:32
msgid "A note on output"
msgstr "Opomba o izhodu"

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid ""
"goat is built to be both a pleasure to use _and_ safe to script. Friendly "
"touches — a 🐐 when everything's green, a hint about your next step — only "
"ever appear on an interactive terminal. Pipe goat into a script or ask for "
"`--json` and you get clean, stable, machine-readable output with nothing "
"decorative in the way. Set `GOAT_NO_FUN=1` and even the interactive "
"flourishes go quiet."
msgstr ""
"goat je zgrajen tako, da je hkrati prijeten za uporabo _in_ varen za "
"skriptiranje. Prijazne podrobnosti — 🐐, ko je vse zeleno, namig o vašem "
"naslednjem koraku — se pojavijo le na interaktivnem terminalu. Preusmerite "
"goat v skript ali zahtevajte `--json` in dobite čist, stabilen, strojno "
"berljiv izhod brez kakršnih koli okraskov v napoto. Nastavite "
"`GOAT_NO_FUN=1` in celo interaktivni okraski utihnejo."

#: src/getting-started.md:3
msgid ""
"You don't need a profile, a bundle, or a network to start. goat ships with a "
"sandbox so you can learn by doing, safely."
msgstr ""
"Za začetek ne potrebujete profila, svežnja ali omrežja. goat se dobavi s "
"peskovnikom, tako da se lahko učite s prakso, varno."

#: src/getting-started.md:5
msgid "1. Say hello"
msgstr "1. Pozdravite"

#: src/getting-started.md:11
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simulated fabric, no real mesh. Run `goat init` to attach a real "
"env.\n"
"goat hello — saying `lo` to the fabric as `default` on topic `hello/"
"default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     accepted topic `hello/default` (simulated)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     routed `lo` to `hello/default` over the WireGuard "
"P2P path (simulated)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber your subscriber received `lo` — round-trip complete "
"(simulated)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: the first message ever sent over a network (ARPANET, 29 Oct 1969) "
"— they typed \"LOGIN\" and the link crashed after two letters.\n"
"round-trip complete.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simuliran fabric, brez resnične mreže. Zaženite `goat init`, da "
"priklopite resnično okolje.\n"
"goat hello — pošiljanje `lo` fabricu kot `default` na temo `hello/default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     sprejel temo `hello/default` (simulirano)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     usmeril `lo` na `hello/default` po poti WireGuard "
"P2P (simulirano)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber vaš naročnik je prejel `lo` — krožno potovanje "
"zaključeno (simulirano)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: prvo sporočilo, ki je bilo kdaj poslano prek omrežja (ARPANET, "
"29. okt. 1969) — vtipkali so \"LOGIN\" in povezava se je sesula po dveh "
"črkah.\n"
"krožno potovanje zaključeno.\n"
"```"

#: src/getting-started.md:21
msgid ""
"`goat hello` publishes a message, subscribes to it, and watches it come back "
"— narrating every hop the data took. In the sandbox those hops are "
"simulated; against a real env they're real. Either way, when it says _round-"
"trip complete_, you know the path works end to end."
msgstr ""
"`goat hello` objavi sporočilo, se naroči nanj in opazuje, kako se vrne — pri "
"tem pripoveduje vsak skok, ki so ga podatki naredili. V peskovniku so ti "
"skoki simulirani; proti resničnemu okolju so resnični. V vsakem primeru, ko "
"reče _krožno potovanje zaključeno_, veste, da pot deluje od konca do konca."

#: src/getting-started.md:23
msgid ""
"The message is `lo` on purpose — the first thing ever sent over a network."
msgstr ""
"Sporočilo je `lo` namenoma — prva stvar, ki je bila kdaj poslana prek "
"omrežja."

#: src/getting-started.md:25
msgid "2. Take the tour"
msgstr "2. Opravite ogled"

#: src/getting-started.md:31
msgid ""
"`goat tutor` is a self-paced, hands-on tour — think `vimtutor` for the "
"fabric. Eight short lessons take you from \"what is this\" to publishing, "
"subscribing, diagnosing, and reading the substrate cascade. It runs in the "
"sandbox by default, saves your place, and you can stop and resume any time:"
msgstr ""
"`goat tutor` je praktičen ogled v lastnem tempu — pomislite na `vimtutor` za "
"fabric. Osem kratkih lekcij vas popelje od \"kaj je to\" do objavljanja, "
"naročanja, diagnosticiranja in branja kaskade substrata. Privzeto teče v "
"peskovniku, shrani vaše mesto, vi pa lahko kadar koli ustavite in "
"nadaljujete:"

#: src/getting-started.md:39
msgid "3. Attach a real environment"
msgstr "3. Priklopite resnično okolje"

#: src/getting-started.md:41
msgid ""
"When you've been issued an onboarding **bundle** (a `.cbor` file with your "
"identity), the wizard takes it from here:"
msgstr ""
"Ko vam je bil izdan **sveženj** za priključitev (datoteka `.cbor` z vašo "
"identiteto), čarovnik prevzame od tu naprej:"

#: src/getting-started.md:49
msgid ""
"`goat init` is the friendly front door — it detects whether you're set up, "
"lets you choose the sandbox or a real env, proves it works, and points you "
"at the tutor. `goat doctor` then runs a stepped reachability check (mesh → "
"router → certificate → portal) and, if anything's wrong, tells you exactly "
"what to fix."
msgstr ""
"`goat init` je prijazna vhodna vrata — zazna, ali ste nastavljeni, vam "
"omogoči izbiro peskovnika ali resničnega okolja, dokaže, da deluje, in vas "
"usmeri k vadnici. `goat doctor` nato izvede stopenjsko preverjanje "
"dosegljivosti (mreža → usmerjevalnik → potrdilo → portal) in, če je kaj "
"narobe, vam natančno pove, kaj popraviti."

#: src/getting-started.md:51
msgid ""
"When all of doctor's steps pass, you'll see a small 🐐 — you're on the "
"fabric."
msgstr ""
"Ko vsi koraki doctorja uspejo, boste videli majhno 🐐 — ste na fabricu."

#: src/getting-started.md:53
msgid "Where to next"
msgstr "Kam naprej"

#: src/getting-started.md:55
msgid "New to the ideas? Read **[How the fabric works](concepts.md)**."
msgstr "Novi pri teh idejah? Preberite **[Kako deluje fabric](concepts.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:56
msgid "Ready to do things? Jump to **[Everyday tasks](everyday.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Pripravljeni na delo? Skočite na **[Vsakodnevna opravila](everyday.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:57
msgid "Something not working? **[Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md)**."
msgstr "Nekaj ne deluje? **[Odpravljanje težav](troubleshooting.md)**."

#: src/concepts.md:3
msgid ""
"You can use goat productively with just three ideas: **identity**, "
"**topics**, and **no broker**. Here they are."
msgstr ""
"goat lahko produktivno uporabljate že s tremi idejami: **identiteta**, "
"**teme** in **brez posrednika**. Tukaj so."

#: src/concepts.md:5
msgid "A mesh you join with an identity"
msgstr "Mreža, ki se ji pridružite z identiteto"

#: src/concepts.md:7
msgid ""
"The fabric is a self-healing mesh. Peers connect **directly** to each other "
"over encrypted WireGuard tunnels — once you're enrolled, your data doesn't "
"route through a central server, and your connections survive a management-"
"plane outage or a flaky uplink."
msgstr ""
"Fabric je samopopravljalna mreža. Vozlišča se povezujejo **neposredno** drug "
"z drugim prek šifriranih tunelov WireGuard — ko ste vpisani, vaši podatki ne "
"potujejo skozi osrednji strežnik, vaše povezave pa preživijo izpad "
"upravljalne ravni ali nestabilno povezavo navzgor."

#: src/concepts.md:9
msgid ""
"You join with an **identity**: an onboarding _bundle_ that carries your "
"certificate, an access token, and where the fabric lives. The fabric admits "
"you by _who you are_, not by a shared password. `goat profile init "
"<bundle.cbor>` installs that identity; you can hold several under different "
"_contexts_ and switch between them."
msgstr ""
"Pridružite se z **identiteto**: _svežnjem_ za priključitev, ki nosi vaše "
"potrdilo, dostopni žeton in to, kje fabric živi. Fabric vas spusti glede na "
"to, _kdo ste_, ne pa glede na skupno geslo. `goat profile init "
"<bundle.cbor>` namesti to identiteto; lahko jih imate več pod različnimi "
"_konteksti_ in preklapljate med njimi."

#: src/concepts.md:19
msgid "Topics: publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Teme: objavljanje in naročanje"

#: src/concepts.md:21
msgid ""
"Data moves on **topics** — slash-delimited paths like `acme/radar1/tracks`. "
"The model is publish/subscribe:"
msgstr ""
"Podatki se gibljejo po **temah** — poteh, ločenih s poševnico, kot je `acme/"
"radar1/tracks`. Model je objavljanje/naročanje:"

#: src/concepts.md:23
msgid "**Publish** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) writes a value to a topic."
msgstr "**Objavljanje** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) zapiše vrednost v temo."

#: src/concepts.md:24
msgid ""
"**Subscribe** (`goat sub <topic>`) receives every value published there, "
"live, as long as you're allowed to read it."
msgstr ""
"**Naročanje** (`goat sub <topic>`) prejme vsako tam objavljeno vrednost v "
"živo, dokler jo smete brati."

#: src/concepts.md:26
msgid ""
"A topic is just a name; you create it (`goat topic create`), publish to it, "
"and anyone permitted can subscribe. `goat hello` is simply a publish and a "
"subscribe wired together so you can watch a value make the round trip."
msgstr ""
"Tema je le ime; ustvarite jo (`goat topic create`), objavljate vanjo, naroči "
"pa se lahko vsak, ki ima dovoljenje. `goat hello` je preprosto objava in "
"naročilo, povezana skupaj, tako da lahko opazujete, kako vrednost opravi "
"krožno potovanje."

#: src/concepts.md:28
msgid "No broker — and why that matters"
msgstr "Brez posrednika — in zakaj je to pomembno"

#: src/concepts.md:30
msgid ""
"There is **no central broker** sitting in the middle of the data path. When "
"you publish, the value flows over the mesh directly to the peers subscribed "
"to it. That's deliberate: it removes the single bottleneck and single point "
"of failure that a broker would be."
msgstr ""
"Sredi podatkovne poti **ni osrednjega posrednika**. Ko objavljate, vrednost "
"teče prek mreže neposredno do vozlišč, ki so naročena nanjo. To je namerno: "
"odpravlja eno samo ozko grlo in eno samo točko odpovedi, ki bi ju "
"predstavljal posrednik."

#: src/concepts.md:32
msgid ""
"A practical consequence: **reads are broad, writes are the cut.** Being able "
"to _read_ a topic is permissive by design; _writing_ to one is governed by "
"your identity. So you'll rarely be surprised by what you can subscribe to, "
"and the integrity of what's published is anchored to who published it."
msgstr ""
"Praktična posledica: **branja so široka, pisanja so meja.** Možnost _branja_ "
"teme je po zasnovi dopustna; _pisanje_ vanjo pa ureja vaša identiteta. Tako "
"boste redko presenečeni nad tem, na kaj se lahko naročite, integriteta "
"objavljenega pa je zasidrana na to, kdo je to objavil."

#: src/concepts.md:34
msgid "Sandbox vs. real"
msgstr "Peskovnik proti resničnemu"

#: src/concepts.md:36
msgid ""
"Everything above has a faithful **in-process simulation** — the sandbox. "
"`goat hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox`, and `goat tutor` exercise the "
"same shapes (a topic, a publish, a round-trip, a verdict) with no network "
"and no identity, so you can learn the model before you touch the real "
"fabric. The sandbox always says so with a `◇ SANDBOX` banner, and it never "
"writes to or reads from a real mesh."
msgstr ""
"Vse zgoraj ima zvesto **simulacijo znotraj procesa** — peskovnik. `goat "
"hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox` in `goat tutor` izvajajo iste oblike "
"(temo, objavo, krožno potovanje, sodbo) brez omrežja in brez identitete, "
"tako da se lahko naučite modela, preden se dotaknete resničnega fabrica. "
"Peskovnik to vedno pove s pasico `◇ SANDBOX` in nikoli ne piše v resnično "
"mrežo ali bere iz nje."

#: src/concepts.md:38
msgid ""
"When you switch to a real env, the _commands don't change_ — only the "
"backing does."
msgstr ""
"Ko preklopite na resnično okolje, se _ukazi ne spremenijo_ — spremeni se le "
"zaledje."

#: src/concepts.md:40
msgid ""
"Want the deeper architecture (the relay fallback, the access model, the "
"audit trail)? Ask your goat administrator for the design references — this "
"guide stays focused on operating the CLI."
msgstr ""
"Želite globljo arhitekturo (rezervna pot prek releja, model dostopa, "
"revizijska sled)? Vprašajte svojega goat administratorja za zasnovne "
"reference — ta vodnik ostaja osredotočen na upravljanje vmesnika CLI."

#: src/everyday.md:3
msgid ""
"The commands you'll actually reach for, as quick recipes. Add `--help` to "
"any of them for the full set of flags, or see the **[Command reference]"
"(reference.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Ukazi, po katerih boste dejansko posegli, kot hitri recepti. Kateremu koli "
"dodajte `--help` za celoten nabor zastavic ali si oglejte **[Referenco "
"ukazov](reference.md)**."

#: src/everyday.md:5
msgid "Check you're connected"
msgstr "Preverite, ali ste povezani"

#: src/everyday.md:12
msgid ""
"`goat doctor` is your first stop whenever something feels off — each step "
"that fails prints a specific remediation. When everything's green, both "
"commands give you a clear all-clear."
msgstr ""
"`goat doctor` je vaša prva postaja, kadar se zdi nekaj narobe — vsak korak, "
"ki ne uspe, izpiše posebno rešitev. Ko je vse zeleno, vam oba ukaza dasta "
"jasen znak, da je vse v redu."

#: src/everyday.md:14
msgid "Publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Objavljanje in naročanje"

#: src/everyday.md:16
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # watch a topic live (Ctrl-C to "
"stop)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # a whole subtree\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # publish a payload\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # opazujte temo v živo (Ctrl-C za "
"ustavitev)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # celotno poddrevo\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # objavite vsebino\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:22
msgid "Want to see the ripple a publish sets off? Add `--narrate`:"
msgstr "Želite videti val, ki ga sproži objava? Dodajte `--narrate`:"

#: src/everyday.md:24
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:28
msgid "Work with topics"
msgstr "Delo s temami"

#: src/everyday.md:30
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # list topics\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # drill into an org/prefix\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # one topic's full record\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # seznam tem\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # poglobite se v organizacijo/"
"predpono\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # celoten zapis ene teme\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:37
msgid ""
"After you create a topic, goat nudges you toward the natural next step "
"(watch it, or publish to it)."
msgstr ""
"Potem ko ustvarite temo, vas goat usmeri k naravnemu naslednjemu koraku "
"(opazujte jo ali objavite vanjo)."

#: src/everyday.md:39
msgid "Diagnose a problem"
msgstr "Diagnosticirajte težavo"

#: src/everyday.md:47
msgid ""
"`inspect` returns findings and the remedy for each — what's wrong and what "
"to do about it."
msgstr ""
"`inspect` vrne ugotovitve in rešitev za vsako — kaj je narobe in kaj storiti "
"glede tega."

#: src/everyday.md:49
msgid "Scripting"
msgstr "Skriptiranje"

#: src/everyday.md:51
msgid ""
"Every command that prints a human view also offers `--json` for a stable, "
"machine-readable one. The JSON form never carries banners, hints, or "
"flourishes, and its shape and your exit code stay constant across releases "
"and languages:"
msgstr ""
"Vsak ukaz, ki izpiše pogled za človeka, ponuja tudi `--json` za stabilen, "
"strojno berljiv pogled. Oblika JSON nikoli ne nosi pasic, namigov ali "
"okraskov, njena oblika in vaša izhodna koda pa ostajata nespremenjeni med "
"izdajami in jeziki:"

#: src/everyday.md:58
msgid "This is the contract: **friendly on a terminal, clean in a pipe.**"
msgstr "To je dogovor: **prijazno na terminalu, čisto v cevovodu.**"

#: src/everyday.md:60
msgid ""
"One caution: `goat status` opens a real session at the router each time it runs, so it is a check you run when you want an answer, not something to poll from a timer. For a trend over time use `goat health` or `goat top`, which read what the goatnet already publishes."
msgstr ""
"Eno opozorilo: `goat status` ob vsakem zagonu odpre pravo sejo do usmerjevalnika, zato je to preverjanje, ki ga zaženete, ko želite odgovor, ne nekaj, kar bi klicali iz časovnika. Za trend skozi čas uporabite `goat health` ali `goat top`, ki bereta, kar goatnet že objavlja."

#: src/install.md:3
msgid ""
"goat is a single self-contained binary — no runtime, no dependencies. It's "
"served mesh-internally from `get.<your-goatnet>` (you're already on the mesh "
"if you can read this), and the version here always matches the binary that "
"surface serves."
msgstr ""
"goat je ena samostojna binarna datoteka — brez izvajalnega okolja, brez "
"odvisnosti. Postreže se znotraj mreže z `get.<your-goatnet>` (če to lahko "
"berete, ste že na mreži), različica tukaj pa se vedno ujema z binarno "
"datoteko, ki jo postreže ta površina."

#: src/install.md:5
msgid "Quick install"
msgstr "Hitra namestitev"

#: src/install.md:7
msgid "**macOS / Linux**"
msgstr "**macOS / Linux**"

#: src/install.md:10
msgid ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"

#: src/install.md:11
msgid "$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"

#: src/install.md:12
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:17
msgid "Make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your `PATH`."
msgstr "Prepričajte se, da je `~/.local/bin` na vašem `PATH`."

#: src/install.md:19
msgid "**Windows (PowerShell)**"
msgstr "**Windows (PowerShell)**"

#: src/install.md:21
msgid ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"

#: src/install.md:26
msgid ""
"Every subcommand works on Windows except `goat client` (the local tunnel "
"daemon), which is Linux/macOS-only."
msgstr ""
"Vsak podukaz deluje na Windows, razen `goat client` (lokalni demon tunela), "
"ki je le za Linux/macOS."

#: src/install.md:28
msgid "Verify the download (recommended)"
msgstr "Preverite prenos (priporočeno)"

#: src/install.md:30
msgid ""
"The download surface publishes a per-binary `*.sha256` and an aggregate "
"`SHA256SUMS`. For a high-assurance install, verify before you run:"
msgstr ""
"Površina za prenos objavlja `*.sha256` za vsako binarno datoteko in zbirno "
"`SHA256SUMS`. Za namestitev z visokim zagotovilom preverite, preden zaženete:"

#: src/install.md:33
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>\""

#: src/install.md:34
msgid "\"$BASE/SHA256SUMS\""
msgstr "\"$BASE/SHA256SUMS\""

#: src/install.md:35
msgid "\"$BASE/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"$BASE/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:35
msgid "# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c   ·   Linux: sha256sum -c\n"
msgstr "# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c   ·   Linux: sha256sum -c\n"

#: src/install.md:41
msgid "Platforms"
msgstr "Platforme"

#: src/install.md:43
msgid "OS"
msgstr "OS"

#: src/install.md:43
msgid "Architectures"
msgstr "Arhitekture"

